Trace the output when the composed strategy object is dynamically swapped at runtime:

```java
interface PrinterEngine {
    String format(String msg);
}
class PlainEngine implements PrinterEngine {
    public String format(String msg) { return msg.toLowerCase(); }
}
class EmphasizedEngine implements PrinterEngine {
    public String format(String msg) { return msg.toUpperCase(); }
}
class TextDocument {
    private PrinterEngine engine;
    TextDocument(PrinterEngine engine) { this.engine = engine; }
    void setEngine(PrinterEngine engine) { this.engine = engine; }
    void print(String text) { System.out.print(engine.format(text) + " "); }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        TextDocument doc = new TextDocument(new PlainEngine());
        doc.print("Java");
        doc.setEngine(new EmphasizedEngine());
        doc.print("Java");
    }
}
```

Analyze the field mutations through shared component references in this code:

```java
class BatteryPack {
    int chargeLevel = 100;
}
class DroneUnit {
    BatteryPack battery;
    DroneUnit(BatteryPack b) { this.battery = b; }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        BatteryPack sharedPack = new BatteryPack();
        DroneUnit droneA = new DroneUnit(sharedPack);
        DroneUnit droneB = new DroneUnit(sharedPack);
        droneA.battery.chargeLevel -= 30;
        System.out.println(droneB.battery.chargeLevel);
    }
}
```

